INSERT INTO `chat_agent_version` (`created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`, `agent_id`, `description`, `chat_model_ids`, `temperature`, `agent_type`, `prompt_template`, `greeting_message`,`params`, `forest_option`)
VALUES
	('2025-09-28 01:00:00.000', '2025-09-28 01:00:00.000', NULL, @agent_id, 'opo判断第一列是否为表头行机器人', '[1]', '0.33', 'prompt',
	'Given the data example {{input1}}, determine whether the first column in the data is the header column of the row table: \n1. Criteria for judgment \n- All cells in the first column are of text type (not numeric/date /ID/ serial number/pure numerical content) \n- The content has clear classification or attribute description (such as "item", "category", "department", etc.) \n- forms a clear "category-numerical" correspondence with the data on the right \n- In financial tables, If it contains classification labels such as "initial number" and "direct material", it is directly recognized as \n\n2. The situation where false is forcibly returned: \n- The first column contains any non-descriptive content such as numbers, dates, serial numbers, ids, etc. \n- The content of the first column cannot form a reasonable classification relationship with the data on the right. \n- The first row is already the column header row and does not have an independent classification function. \n- The first row contains descriptive column headings (such as "Month", "Sales Volume", "year-on-year growth Rate"), and the content of the first column is data items that can be interpreted by the column headings (such as "January", "February", which belong to the specific values of "Month") \n3. Priority description \n- When the first column contains obvious classification labels such as "item" and "category", it is preferentially recognized as a row header \n- For tables with obvious transposible structures (descriptive content in the first column + multiple columns of numerical data), it is directly recognized \n- When there are dual headers (both rows and columns are described), it is determined by whether the content in the first column constitutes an independent classification \n\n The result only returns a Boolean value.',
	'',
    '[{"input":"input1","name":"数据","description":"数据","is_title":true,"input_type":"text","input_array":[],"is_required":false}]',
    '{"prompt_template":"","doc_forest_ids":null}');
